From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: the index kernels take decode windows (TF_GLM_INDEX_CUDA)

ai-engine ab3009315 + 868689925 (grafted; comment lines single-lined for the lean rule).

A decode window re-reads every pooled key a row in tf_glm_scores (one row a block):
at 596k tokens that is about 38 MB a row a DSA layer. TF_GLM_INDEX_CUDA=all routes
windows of any row count through glm_index_scores (rows share each staged 64-pool
tile) and glm_index_pools (the floor select); 1 keeps its prompt-chunk-only meaning.
TF_GLM_INDEX_DECODE_FROM gates a window by depth, read once at load; 0 keeps every
depth. Measurement (ai-engine docs/SPEEDUPS.md): INDEX_CUDA=1 cold 267k -2.2 pct,
133k -1.1 pct, byte-equal gate; the =all extension rides the same kernels. Default off.

Gates on pin+0001..0005: check-native-cuda-host green, whole-tree fmt green, lean
base-vs-head 0 new. No .cu change: the kernels are upstream pin code; this patch
only routes windows to them.

